      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T16:05:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hau, I was looking at this today and realized what the problem is: the syntax for initializing round_consts should not have \u003c\u003e angle brackets; the actual table in memory is not properly initialized, so the iterations are using round constants of all zeros. Making this change:\n\n```\n-DATA   round_consts\u003c\u003e+0x00(SB)/8, $0x0000000000000001\n-DATA   round_consts\u003c\u003e+0x08(SB)/8, $0x0000000000008082\n+DATA   round_consts+0x00(SB)/8, $0x0000000000000001\n+DATA   round_consts+0x08(SB)/8, $0x0000000000008082\n```\n\netc etc, passes the tests for me. Thanks for doing the work on this BTW!",
      "parentUuid": "82c80846_0b3a8bba",
      "revId": "337ab28b395c2cf858fc9ff4c7a9e6d554cd50d9",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
